# Desktop Filler Notice

The default desktop DOM engine reuses core.js, repeater-engine.js and content.js
from the user's local resume-filler browser extension, version 0.11.5. File hashes
and provenance are recorded in browser-engine/provenance.json (upstream hashes).
Local content.js patches: native-select verification uses the selected option value
instead of comparing an internal value against its display label; desktop repeat
preparation accepts only validated add-only plans and checks cancellation/deadlines
between additions, without invoking the extension's full-page prepare defaults.
Read-only registration context can disable host-name fallback; desktop drafts use
the original company/title extractors without guessing company names from domains.
Explicitly branded recruitment titles take priority over loose header/navigation text.
Company-label cleanup also removes the leading Chinese welcome-to-join phrase.
The desktop safety
adapter and compact compatibility engine are maintained separately in index.cjs.
No original license file was supplied. This notice records provenance, not a new
license grant; confirm the source owner's redistribution rights before publishing.

The import excludes personal resume data, browser storage, attachments, service
bindings, cookies, tokens, background and SMS/native-messaging components. Dormant
extension message branches are not exposed by the desktop's allowlisted dispatcher.

`loadLocalFiller()` remains an optional compatibility adapter for a user-selected,
trusted local source directory. It is not used by the packaged default workflow and
does not grant any license to redistribute that selected source.

The bundled engine never handles passwords, SMS/OTP fields, CAPTCHA, or final form
submission. File upload and field filling require an explicit user action. Website
compatibility varies and must be reported as supported, partial, or unsupported.
